I've been playing roguelikes since about 1990 (Nethack since 1992), and
never beaten one without cheating in one form or another.  I simply
loved the punishment and pain too much to quit.

I am pleased to announce that this has changed today.

I may have spoiled the hell out of the game, knowing every trick, in,
and out, and it was still hard as all get out.

This particular character has been played for about two weeks now,
because I always die when I'm tired (on tilt?).  Consequently, I don't
remember a whole lot about it.

As usual, neutral human male archaeologist.  Started with the basic
assortment of gear, no oil lamp or marker.  Hacked my way down to
Minetown, scooping up dwarvish mithril and a mattock.  I did find
several Vaults while in the main dungeons, and put that money to good
use buying protection--and lots of it.

Found a scroll of genocide, promptly wiped out 'h'--I have a bones
level with three promising characters killed by a MMF on the 9th level
of the Mines.

Found a bag of holding sitting on the floor in the dungeon, did Sokoban
anyway and got another one.

Finally found an altar around dlevel 11, did my water prayer.  No
scrolls of enchant anything so far, still got my basic dwarvish
mithril/hard shoes/hard hat/mattock setup.  Blessed some scrolls of ID
to identify all the scrolls and wands kicking around in my inventory.
Got a magic lamp that I kept as a light source and an oilskin cloak.
Found some +2 gloves.

Finally hit xplevel 14 (a rarity for me) and went in to do my quest.
Almost lost it, luckily a potion of full healing saved the day and the
Bell and Orb were mine.

Finally found an enchant weapon scroll, got my mattock up to +3 and
rustproofed.

After a few close calls with soldiers and wands of fire, got to Medusa,
but no ring of levitation.  Dug down and came up next to her, towel
wrapped around my head.  Showed her my looking glass and that was that.
 Busted up the statue and got myself a polished silver shield that
saved my bacon many times.

Kept on truckin, despite losing my gloves to a lich.  Genocided them
shortly after.  A lucky throne sit netted me GDSM (+0...probably
shouldn't have wished for +5).
Finally made it to the Castle, a feat I've only accomplished twice
before without cheating.  Played my flute until the drawbridge dropped.
 Actually kicked everything's ass, surprisingly--having genocided L
helped a great deal.  Started practicing with the silver saber I took
off a dead lieutenant.

Got the wand, wished for Grayswandir.  Dropped through the trapdoor,
hit Gehennom.  Never been this far legitimately.  Bought off the
demons.  Juiblex almost got me, I was diseased inside him and
accidentally attacked again--luckily I was able to get my full healing
potion out and drink it in time.  Remembered the digging trick, beat
him down.  Couldn't advance, spent some time going up and down, finally
had to burn a wish on a ring of levitation.  Used another one on a
scroll of charging, charged up the wand again.

By this time I was expert in saber and twoweaponing silver sabers
thanks to the amulet of reflection I found.  Yeenhogu decided to pop in
and say hi, but he was a pushover.  I finally found the ladder to
Vlad's tower after a great deal of searching, killed everything in
there.

Unfortunately, by the time I had hit the first fake tower, my AC was
still poor (-10 or so) and I did not have cold or fire resistance
intrinsically.  Spent a couple of days walking around, farming scrolls,
used a wish on a magic marker and got myself down to -25.  Found speed
boots and a cornuthaum.

Three boneheaded mistakes almost lost the game for me.  One, I quaffed
one of two unidentified potions left without remembering it could be
polymorph--turned into a gray dragon and ripped my +3 oilskin cloak.
Shit.  Shortly after I went over to the wizard's tower but still had my
speed boots on--not water walking.  Erased my scroll of taming, remove
curse, most of my potions, etc. etc.  Gave me 22 scrolls of blank paper
to work with, but no magic marker.  Thirdly, attempting to perform
alchemy, I dipped my 6 extra healing potions into gain level--turning
them to water.

Went back up and found a cloak of invisibility, figured that would see
me through.  AC was about -32.  Finally decided to go for it, killed
the Wizard.  He wasn't too bad, the twoweaponing really helped.  The
priestess took some more work, but the ring of conflict I got made it a
bit easier.

Charged back up through the levels, but got sent back down a LOT.
Stupid mysterious force.  Killed the Wizard a few more times, lots of
double trouble.  Never did anything but hand to hand, he couldn't get
through my AC.  Once I left Gehennom it was a breeze up to the planes.


Bit my lip, took a breath, and went up dlevel1 stairs.  Hit Earth.
Realized I had forgotten the orb of detection, it was taken by the
Wizard and I never got it back.  Oops.  The Wizard showed up, wasn't
really too difficult to kill him.  Used one of my two scrolls of gold
detection and a faded magic missile spell to locate the portal after
searching for 30 minutes with a pickaxe and three wands of digging.
Left my trusty mattock behind and hit it.

I was worried about the air elementals, but they really weren't that
bad.  When several surrounded me I had to use a few wand of death
charges and a couple of teleports, nothing major.  Used my other gold
detection to get the hell out of there.

Fire was easy, although the Wizard put in another appearance.  Walked
around until I found the portal on the left side on the bottom.

Water wasn't too bad, although I was nervous about being drowned since
I had no magic breathing or oil or grease.  Wasn't a problem, I was
never grabbed.  Took a while to blindly find the portal.  Had to check
the spoilers to find out where it lived (I wasted a lot of time not
moving between bubbles).

Astral Plane.  I was worried about the Riders, I REALLY didn't want to
die.  My angel got eaten by a worm, so I said the hell with it and put
on my conflict ring.  All hell broke loose.  Deathrayed Famine twice,
fought my way to the wrong altar in the center.  Damn.  A lieutenant
summoned by a priestess did me a favor and killed Famine twice with his
longsword.  I had to have Famine chase me around the altar room a few
times so I could escape.

Went left.  Saw people dropping like flies and knew it was Pestilence.
Shot him with the deathray and fought my way in.  I noticed that
monsters started fleeing as soon as I hit the altar room, so I pulled
off my ring of conflict.  I couldn't get the high priestess to move off
the altar, she was too busy fighting.  Nobody was really hurting me, so
I waited it out.  Hopped on the altar, #offered....and thus my first
ascension.  Didn't use half my emergency gear (K-rations, full healing
potions, all sorts of wands)--just two full healing potions and a wand
of death.

